# rule.always.hunt-the-serialization-when-you-rank
every time you rank a goal, hunt its neighborhood for work that runs in SERIES and could run in PARALLEL — and state what you found, in the same turn. method: `howto.find-the-serialization-a-rank-hides.md`.
fires on: `eco.priority set` on a new row · a re-grade (sev, urg, sponsorship) · a decomposition (children default to a chain unless you say otherwise — the sharpest moment) · a gate edge set or struck · "can these run together?" · a seed dispatched · the phrase "and then we do X".
why ALWAYS: skipped, no column goes wrong — the loss is wall-clock, so the only evidence a hunt happened is that the turn said so. and a rank is when the neighborhood is already loaded.
the turn owes one sentence per rank — e.g. "the three peers are already parallel — none gated, all seeded" · "found one: X was never dispatched; seeded" · "the fold stays — the grove is at cap". a clean hunt is still stated. a find left uncured is named, with what holds it.
cues: you finish an `eco.priority set` and move on → stop, what did the hunt return? · a `--gated-by` → is it an OUTPUT dependency or a preference? · children → default PARALLEL, a reason per chain edge · siblings all at one sev → was a measurement available? · "once X lands, then Y" → write it as an edge, or strike it · three clean hunts straight → did you check only `gatedBy`? two of three serializers aren't edges.
test: can I name the OUTPUT each edge waits on? no → it costs a peer's full duration; strike it or record why.
bound: a hunt of the touched neighborhood, never a full-store sweep. to find is mandatory; to fan out is a judgment (the grove is capped), stated in the `--why`.
blocker: a rank set or moved with no hunt stated · children chained with no reason per edge · a find left unstated · a hunt that checks `gatedBy` alone and reports clean. nitpick: a kept gate edge with no reason in `--why` · a rank that stalls into a full-store audit.
see also: `howto.find-the-serialization-a-rank-hides` · `rule.require.a-gain-cell-behind-every-sev` · `rule.forbid.fabricated-opines` · `rule.always.prioritize-never-supervise` · `define.invariant.eco.a-part-gates-its-whole` · `rule.require.bound-grove-concurrency-by-saturation` (supervisor). the argument and evidence: `rule.always.hunt-the-serialization-when-you-rank.md`, beside this file.